6.3 API layer rules (src/services, src/adapters)
One apiClient (fetch wrapper): base URL, credentials: 'include' for cookie sessions, JSON/multipart handling, timeouts via AbortController, retries only for idempotent GETs (max 2, jittered), Idempotency-Key (crypto.randomUUID()) on POST /ingestion/jobs and POST /answers, CSRF header on state-changing requests (read the token the backend provides), upload progress via XMLHttpRequest.
Envelope: success {data, meta{request_id,next_cursor,total_estimate,scope}}; error {error{code,message,details,request_id}}. Map every error code to a specific, human message and component state (AUTH_REQUIRED → sign-in; FORBIDDEN → "not permitted for your role"; NOT_FOUND → neutral "not available"; RATE_LIMITED → show retry-after; DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE/UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT → service-unavailable state with retry; VALIDATION_ERROR → field messages). Always surface request_id in error states.
Validation: zod schemas mirroring the interfaces in §6.5, lenient (unknown fields allowed; missing optional fields safe). On parse failure show "The service returned an unexpected response" with a Retry and log details to the console; never crash and never render partial garbage.
Pagination: cursor-based (limit, cursor); limit ≤ 100; show page controls and total estimate when provided.
Normalisers at the service boundary: convert the brief's legacy answer shape (answer, claims[].source_email_ids, sources[], limitations[]) into the internal Answer; accept conditions as strings or objects; accept missing provenance (treat as EXPLICIT only if the backend says so, otherwise show "provenance not reported").
Two adapters, one interface (DataSource): liveAdapter (HTTP) and demoAdapter (reads src/data/demoData.ts). The mode is chosen by VITE_DATA_MODE and, if allowed, the Settings switch (persisted in localStorage). There is no automatic fallback from live to demo. In live mode with the backend offline show the ServiceUnavailable state (with the configured base URL, GET health result and a Retry).
Demo mode banner (persistent, top of every workspace page, not dismissible): "Demo dataset — the supplied synthetic benchmark with pre-authored annotations. Not live backend output." Every KPI and chart derived from demo data carries a small "Demo annotation" source label.
6.4 Demo adapter behaviour
Load sutra_demo_data.json (attached) into src/data/demoData.ts as a typed constant (DemoDataset, §6.5) — convert the JSON verbatim; do not rewrite, shorten, translate or "improve" any email text, quote or annotation.
emails/threads/decisions/actions/summaries/attachments: support the same filters, sorting and cursor pagination as the live contract, computed in memory.
Personas (personas[]): a persona picker on the sign-in screen. If a persona has an address, filter threads/emails/ledger to threads where that address is sender or recipient of any message ("thread participant" policy); personas without an address (inst.admin, sysadmin, compliance) see all threads in demo only for illustration. Label: "Demo persona — visibility illustrated in the browser, not enforced."
search in demo mode is a plain client-side keyword filter over emails, attachments, threads, decisions and actions. Label it "Demo keyword search (not AI retrieval)".
answers in demo mode: match the submitted question (case/whitespace/punctuation-insensitive) and optional thread_scope against answers[].matches[]; return that pre-authored Answer. If nothing matches, return a truthful message: "Demo mode answers the suggested questions only. Connect the backend (live mode) to ask free-form questions." — never invent an answer. Clarification answers carry options[]; clicking an option re-submits {question, thread_scope}. Every demo answer displays a "Pre-authored demo answer — not generated by a model" tag.
ingestion: the preloaded job job-demo-benchmark is shown in history. A new upload in demo mode performs only the in-browser pre-check (§7 Page 8) and states: "Processing requires the backend. This is a browser-side pre-check." No pipeline step is shown as complete.
Time-of-day greeting uses the browser clock; the user name is the persona's display_name. Never invent a real person's name.
