Breakpoints: ≥1280 desktop (primary), 1024–1279 laptop, 768–1023 tablet, <768 mobile. Sidebars → drawers; evidence panels stack below answers or become bottom sheets; tables scroll horizontally inside their own container or convert to structured cards on mobile; no page-level horizontal overflow at any width; keep all major functionality on mobile.
WCAG 2.2 AA: semantic landmarks (header, nav, main, aside, footer), skip-to-content link, one h1 per page, tables with caption and header scope, labelled form fields, aria-live="polite" for answers/toasts/status changes, visible focus everywhere, keyboard operation of every control (drawers trap focus, menus follow listbox/menu patterns), minimum 44×44 px touch targets, colour never the only signal, prefers-reduced-motion honoured, lang="en", correct language handling for Devanagari text.
Performance: route-level code splitting; 3D lazily loaded and only when visible; no autoplay video; avoid heavy libraries; memoise lists; paginate (don't render unbounded lists); stable component identities; images/SVG optimised; no layout shift from fonts; no console errors or warnings; zero TypeScript errors under strict.
